 attributes are the propeties of the class and 
 methods are the functions of the class.

we represent these classes in the UML diagram.

the class is represented in the UML diagram with a rectangle which has three parts
1. the first part is the name of the class
2. the second part is the attributes of the class
3. the third part is the methods of the class    

+ means public
- means private
# means protected


class Car {
    //Attributes
    private String brand;
    private int year;

    // Constructor is a function which calls by default just when the object is created
    //So if we want to give some default values to the attributes of the class we can do it in the constructor
    public Car(String brand, int year) {
        this.brand = brand;
        this.year = year;
    }

    // Methods
    public void displayDetails() {
        System.out.println("Car: " + this.brand + ", Year: " + this.year);
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Car car1 = new Car("Toyota", 2022);
        Car car2 = new Car("Honda", 2025);
        car1.displayDetails();
        car2.displayDetails();
    }
}

